in tumor treatment on pathological delta activity in MEG</article-title><source>NeuroImage</source><year>2003</year><volume>20</volume><fpage>2291</fpage><lpage>2301</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14683730</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.neuroimage.2003.07.030</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Vieth</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Kober</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Gummich</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Sources of spontaneous slow waves associated with brain lesions, localized by using the MEG</article-title><source>Brain Topography</source><year>1996</year><volume>8</volume><fpage>215</fpage><lpage>221</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8728406</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1007/BF01184772</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Vieth</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Kober</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Kamada</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Ganslandt</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Koga Y et al</surname></name></person-group><article-title>Normal and abnormal MEG activity in border zones of brain lesions</article-title><source>Brain Topography Today</source><year>1998</year><publisher-name>Amsterdam: Elsevier</publisher-name><fpage>39</fpage><lpage>46</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Vieth</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Kober</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Ganslandt</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>M&#x000f6;ller</surname><given-names>M